      "schema:description": "Distinguish pretraining, supervised fine-tuning on instruction-response pairs, preference-based methods (reward-model RLHF and direct preference optimization), and parameter-efficient adaptation at the level of what data, targets and parameters change; explain model-specific conversation serialization through chat templates; contrast these with in-context learning and retrieval-augmented generation. Algorithms (PPO, DPO objective derivations), recipes of particular models and evaluation of assistant behaviour are out of scope.",
      "schema:inLanguage": "en",
      "schema:learningResourceType": "concept-lesson",
      "schema:name": "From a base model to an assistant: post-training"
    },
